'''Muthoot Pappachan Group''', also known as '''Muthoot Blue''', is an Indian financial service [[Conglomerate (company)|conglomerate]] founded in 1887 by [[Muthoot Family|Ninan Mathai Muthoot]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.financialexpress.com/industry/muthoot-fincorp-rolls-out-5th-tranche-of-rs-900-crore-capital-market-plan/1817381/|title=Muthoot Fincorp rolls out 5th tranche of Rs 900-crore capital market plan|date=2020-01-09|website=The Financial Express|language=en-US|access-date=2020-02-12}}</ref><ref name=":1">{{Cite web|url=https://www.fortuneindia.com/enterprise/muthoot-pappachan-group-riding-out-the-storm/103841|title=Muthoot Pappachan Group: Riding out the storm|website=fortuneindia.com|language=en|access-date=2020-02-12}}</ref><ref name=":0">{{Cite web|url=https://www.livemint.com/Companies/l3tBBv1zUaiHcmOa1Q0tvO/Muthoot-Pappachan-Group-goes-back-to-roots-with-planned-micr.html|title=Muthoot Pappachan Group goes back to roots with planned microfinance unit|last=Sanjai|first=Vishwanath Nair, P R.|date=2015-05-01|website=Livemint|language=en|access-date=2020-02-12}}</ref> Headquartered in [[Thiruvananthapuram]], [[Kerala]], the group has a workforce of more than 26,000 employees across 4,200 branches in India.<ref name=":2">{{Cite web|url=http://www.forbesindia.com/article/boardroom/the-other-muthoot-true-blue-heirs/51265/1|title=The Other Muthoot: True Blue Heirs|website=Forbes India|language=en|access-date=2020-02-12}}</ref><ref name=":3">{{Cite news|last=Sangani|first=Priyanka|url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/tech/ites/muthoot-pappachan-group-ties-up-with-ust-global-for-digital-transformation-initiative/articleshow/74064469.cms?from=mdr|title=Muthoot Pappachan Group ties up with UST Global for digital transformation initiative|date=2020-02-10|work=The Economic Times|access-date=2020-02-12}}</ref> Apart from financial services, the group has business interests in hospitality, automotive dealerships, real estate, healthcare, IT services, precious metals, alternate energy, and security services.<ref name=":0" /><ref>{{cite news |title=Muthoot Pappachan Group aims to double wind energy generation capacity by end 2012 |url=https://www.business-standard.com/article/press-releases/muthoot-pappachan-group-aims-to-double-wind-energy-generation-capacity-by-end-2012-110111500114_1.html |access-date=11 February 2023 |work=Business Standard India |date=15 November 2010}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Lele |first1=Abhijit |title=Muthoot Fincorp promoters to expand real estate business |url=https://www.business-standard.com/article/companies/muthoot-fincorp-promoters-to-expand-real-estate-business-115071100259_1.html |access-date=11 February 2023 |work=Business Standard India |date=11 July 2015}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Muthoot Pappachan Group to widen security initiative |url=https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/news/national/muthoot-pappachan-group-to-widen-security-initiative/article8102706.ece |access-date=11 February 2023 |work=Business Line|location=Chennai |date=13 January 2016 |language=en}}</ref>

==History==
The family business was founded in 1887 by M. N. Mathai Muthoot in [[Kozhencherry]], [[Kerala]].<ref name=":2" /><ref>{{Cite news|last=Muthoot|first=MG George|url=https://www.business-standard.com/article/management/40-years-ago-and-now-pushing-for-growth-114112300667_1.html|title=40 Years Ago... and now: Pushing for growth|date=2014-11-24|work=Business Standard India|access-date=2020-02-12}}</ref> Mathai initially traded in timber and food grains, supplying rations to large British-run plantations.

In 1939, the group established banking and finance services to provide immediate financial assistance to customers in rural and non-rural areas through easy secured loans.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.forbes.com/global/2011/1107/india-billionaires-11-george-muthoot-hoarders-kuttickat-rai.html|title=Indian Billionaire George Muthoot's Pot of Gold|last=Rai|first=Saritha|date=26 October 2011|magazine=Forbes|language=en|access-date=2020-02-12}}</ref> Post-independence, the demand for credit increased as individuals discovered their household gold as a safe and convenient means to get credit. Mathai then moved into the gold loan business.

In 1979, the business was split among the founder's three surviving sons. The eldest son, [[M George Muthoot|M. George Muthoot]], moved out of [[Kerala]] and set up [[Muthoot Finance]]. The youngest son, M. Thomas Muthoot, also known as Muthoot Pappachan, then incorporated Muthoot Pappachan Group.<ref name=":2" /><ref name=":1"/> The group is currently under his three sons T. John Muthoot, T. George Muthoot and T. Thomas Muthoot (known as just Thomas Muthoot).

In May 2024, the group signed [[Shah Rukh Khan]] as a brand ambassador.<ref name=":2" /><ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/money-and-banking/shah-rukh-khan-new-brand-ambassador-of-muthoot-pappachan-group/article68232564.ece|title=Shah Rukh Khan, new brand ambassador of Muthoot Pappachan Group
|work=Business Line|location=Chennai|access-date=2024-08-24}}</ref>

